{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014T1kGyDrqV5KNSt4ACJ8Kj","type":"tool_result","content":"30:game.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\n31:game.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n274:- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpa\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a \n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n287:- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n290:- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the direction changes or a button is presse\n291:- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or\n294:- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '62\n296:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n301:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n302:- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the co\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n314:- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n315:- `input.tick(dt)`: advance input by one step: read the gamepad and turn presses since the last step into this step's pressed() and released() (the engine calls it every step)\n317:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { j\n319:- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n323:- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n325:- `input.deadzone = .18`: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n333:- `input.pad = 'any'` †: the gamepad this input reads: 'any' (the first connected one another player hasn't: player 1's), an index (a joined player's own), or null (none)\n335:- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n336:- `input.padId = ''`, `input.padIndex = null`: the gamepad in use (null and '' without one)\n337:- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n338:- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n339:- `input.padPrev = []`: which gamepad buttons were down at the last step\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit }))\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', ru\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls'\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone'\n530:- `game.input`: keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, read as actions (pressed, down, move, ...)\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.click\n1095:- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and s\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); \n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1340:- `E.FIGHT_KEYS: up, down, left, right, lp, hp, lk, hk, start, pause, confirm, cancel` †: the fighting preset (a scene's input): the moves and menu keys of E.Input.DEFAULT, light and heavy punch (U, I; a pad's X, Y), light and heavy kick (J, K; A, B)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-054528__x4cdb93/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"799c6357-620a-439f-ad68-1731060eb345","uuid":"ffbb5221-c427-4714-87d7-b69f9ca84840","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:46:42.235Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"30:game.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\n31:game.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n274:- `E.Input.THIRDPERSON { sprint, jump, crouch, interact, attack, block, dodge, use, map }` †: third-person action and stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear): WASD / stick move, Shift sprint, Space jump and parkour, C crouch (a toggle), E interact, J attack\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpa\n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a \n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n287:- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n290:- `input.history` †: the last second of input, oldest first: [{ t (input.clock), dir (numpad 1-9 for a fighter facing right: 5 neutral), pressed: the actions pressed then, directions aside }], one entry each time the direction changes or a button is presse\n291:- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or\n294:- `input.motion(digits, button, o = {})` †: a fighter's move in numpad notation, mirrored by facing: input.motion('236', 'attack', { facing: hero.facing, window }) is a quarter circle forward and punch (down, down-forward, forward, attack: a fireball); '62\n296:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n301:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n302:- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Returns null when done, the action that already uses the co\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n314:- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n315:- `input.tick(dt)`: advance input by one step: read the gamepad and turn presses since the last step into this step's pressed() and released() (the engine calls it every step)\n317:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { j\n319:- `input.unbind(a, device)` †: take away action a's codes for one device ('keys' or 'pad'); the arrow keys and d-pad stay on the moves\n323:- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\n325:- `input.deadzone = .18`: how far a gamepad stick moves before it counts (0..0.8)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n333:- `input.pad = 'any'` †: the gamepad this input reads: 'any' (the first connected one another player hasn't: player 1's), an index (a joined player's own), or null (none)\n335:- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n336:- `input.padId = ''`, `input.padIndex = null`: the gamepad in use (null and '' without one)\n337:- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n338:- `input.padMove = [0, 0]`: the gamepad's left stick after the dead zone\n339:- `input.padPrev = []`: which gamepad buttons were down at the last step\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit }))\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', ru\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls'\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone'\n530:- `game.input`: keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, read as actions (pressed, down, move, ...)\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.click\n1095:- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and s\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); \n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1340:- `E.FIGHT_KEYS: up, down, left, right, lp, hp, lk, hk, start, pause, confirm, cancel` †: the fighting preset (a scene's input): the moves and menu keys of E.Input.DEFAULT, light and heavy punch (U, I; a pad's X, Y), light and heavy kick (J, K; A, B)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /h