{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwN4gsmqDzQxq5FPLih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The About screen fits, though the page-turn hint shows \"LEFTRIGHT\" because of a missing separator. I'll fix that. Then I'll write the final feedback answers into `build/feedback.json`. They come from what actually happened in this run, and the same file feeds the About screen and `exit-interview.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1605,"cache_read_input_tokens":314375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1605},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"799c6357-620a-439f-ad68-1731060eb345","uuid":"b16766e1-4c99-4abc-b30e-4824413d8177","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:06:51.788Z","request_id":"req_011CghwN4KoSFxCqGf2wBEwh"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwN4gsmqDzQxq5FPLih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UpfvzMRf7X14RhsYqxc86U","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i \"s/GAME.input.label('left') + GAME.input.label('right') + ' TURN PAGE/GAME.input.label('left') + '\\/' + GAME.input.label('right') + ' TURN PAGE/\" src/50-ui.js && grep -c \"label('left') + '/'\" src/50-ui.js && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='build/feedback.json'\nf=json.load(open(p))\nf['sourceInformation'].update({\n \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\n \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape), with a trophy encounter and bonus games\",\n \"perspective\": \"First person, on rails: a fixed vantage per site over a pseudo-3D landscape, with an x-ray Shot Chart in the tallies and 2D menus\",\n \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (unmodified; canvas 2D with its pixel primitives, scenes, input, standard menus and synth audio), AI Hub client lib/hub session.js 1.4.0 (verbatim, ghost mode), vanilla JavaScript, Node 24 for build and tests, Playwright (Chromium) for the browser pass\",\n \"artDirection\": \"The engine's retro-modern pixel style: procedural landscapes per hunt (autumn creek, alpine ridge, snowy muskeg), animals and critters painted from primitives, a 5x7 pixel font\",\n \"animation\": \"Procedural in code: gait from walking speed, grazing, bolting, staring when called, falling when shot. The engine's Humanoid and Quadruped rigs were not used\",\n \"audio\": \"Bluegrass chiptune songs, gunshots, bugle call and bird chirps, and gibberish Animalese voices for the cast, all synthesized in code (engine chip synth); no audio files\",\n \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode: reticles sent between up to four copies; progress and a single result reported to the hub\",\n \"testing\": \"Node tests (node tests/run.mjs) drive the game with game.advance and game.debug, including a scripted whole-campaign playthrough; a Chromium pass over every screen (tests/browser.py); the AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players with latency, jitter and loss\",\n \"research\": \"Read the Big Buck Hunter and Big Buck Hunter Pro pages during planning (PLAN.md section 1.1); nothing new searched while building\",\n \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium for the browser checks; browser for the player unknown\",\n \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n \"usage\": \"unknown\",\n})\nf['testingFeedback'] = [\n \"About 9 game issues: 1 critical (the results screen threw after the last segment, so a finished Hunt-Off showed the engine's error panel and could not be saved); 8 smaller (prompt glyphs showing as '?', a caption over the rifle panel, Dev mode rows running into the hint line, antlers above the Shot Chart frame, an empty bar on the doe-rule choice, a shot-into-a-doe bug that benched the attract bot's gun, a crash when firing outside a site, and menu idle not starting attract). Most were found in the browser pass and screenshots.\",\n \"Critical: the results-screen crash, found by a screenshot after the campaign ended, not by the Node tests, which had passed. Game-breaking for the campaign ending; fixed and covered by the browser pass.\",\n \"Most helpful: the browser pass that opens every screen and takes screenshots. It caught the crash and the visual faults the Node checks could not see.\",\n \"Least helpful: the same-seed determinism check. It only confirms the seeded streams repeat, and passed on the first run. The AI Hub harness was more useful: it checked the real protocol with a real client.\",\n]\nf['engineFeedback'] = [\n \"Liked most: the overlay and pixel primitives (r.overlay with px.rect, poly, ell and font.text) made a custom pseudo-3D scene easy; and the standard pause, settings, controls and full screen menus came free.\",\n \"Stuck or guessed wrong: scene changes fade, so a key sent right after one lands on the old scene (tests need about 0.6 s of settling); a scripted tap sets the last device to touch, so input.label() shows action names; the font has no middle dot or en dash, so they print as '?'. I guessed E.mix and E.font.wrap from the index and confirmed both by running them.\",\n \"Most important thing built myself: the hunt itself. The landscape painter, the animal rigs, the hit zones and shot resolution, the pump and chamber model, the bot, the x-ray Shot Chart and the bonus games. The engine's depth, lighting and camera were bypassed for an overlay-drawn scene.\",\n \"Hardest part: fitting an on-rails, screen-space shooter into an engine built around its camera views and lit scenes; the overlay gets no depth sort, lighting or shadows for free.\",\n \"Changes to the engine: none. The engine file is the handoff copy, unmodified.\",\n \"One change I'd make: label() should fall back to the keyboard's names when the last device is a scripted tap, and the font should cover the middle dot and en dash.\",\n]\nf['promptFeedback'] = [\n \"Liked most: the explicit core loop, the one-line deliverable names, and the testing rules (game.advance, game.debug, one command that prints only failures). They made the work concrete.\",\n \"Confusing: PLAN.md names a different title and dev folder from TASK.md, and describes about 30 source files and a 17-minute, three-hunt game with a voxel renderer. TASK.md wins on conflicts, but the scale was hard to reconcile with one session, so I built the plan's systems in a smaller form.\",\n \"Hardest: keeping to the plan's scope while finishing a complete, playable slice in one session, and writing the usage and feedback answers accurately without measurements.\",\n \"Change: say up front how much of the plan is required versus illustrative, give a scope budget for one session, and say whether the title should come from the plan or be drawn fresh.\",\n]\nf['aiHub'].update({\n \"series\": \"Big Buck Hunter\",\n \"players\": \"1-4\",\n \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\"],\n \"controls\": \"Aim: mouse or left stick. Shoot: click, Space or R2. Pump: R or Square. Scope: hold Shift or right click. Call: C or Triangle.\"\n})\njson.dump(f, open(p,'w'), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('feedback written')\nEOF\nnode build/build.mjs && timeout 600 node tests/run.mjs | tail -3 && python3 -c \"import json; j=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json')); print(sorted(j.keys())); print(len(j['testingFeedback']), len(j['engineFeedback']), len(j['promptFeedback']))\"","description":"Write final feedback, rebuild, rerun tests, validate interview"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1605,"cache_read_input_tokens":314375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1605},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"799c6357-620a-439f-ad68-1731060eb345","uuid":"d2cfbbfc-a291-4db6-9f10-63db97f31210","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:07:03.122Z","request_id":"req_011CghwN4KoSFxCqGf2wBEwh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UpfvzMRf7X14RhsYqxc86U":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-054528__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHunterHoedown-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-054528 && sed -i \"s/GAME.input.label('left') + GAME.input.label('right') + ' TURN PAGE/GAME.input.label('left') + '\\/' + GAME.input.label('right') + ' TURN PAGE/\" src/50-ui.js && grep -c \"label('left') + '/'\" src/50-ui.js && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='build/feedback.json'\nf=json.load(open(p))\nf['sourceInformation'].update({\n \"source\": \"Big Buck Hunter Pro\",\n \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n \"genre\": \"Arcade light-gun hunting shooter (a shooting gallery in a living landscape), with a trophy encounter and bonus games\",\n \"perspective\": \"First person, on rails: a fixed vantage per site over a pseudo-3D landscape, with an x-ray Shot Chart in the tallies and 2D menus\",\n \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (unmodified; canvas 2D with its pixel primitives, scenes, input, standard menus and synth audio), AI Hub client lib/hub session.js 1.4.0 (verbatim, ghost mode), vanilla JavaScript, Node 24 for build and tests, Playwright (Chromium) for the browser pass\",\n \"artDirection\": \"The engine's retro-modern pixel style: procedural landscapes per hunt (autumn creek, alpine ridge, snowy muskeg), animals and critters painted from primitives, a 5x7 pixel font\",\n \"animation\": \"Procedural in code: gait from walking speed, grazing, bolting, staring when called, falling when shot. The engine's Humanoid and Quadruped rigs were not used\",\n \"audio\": \"Bluegrass chiptune songs, gunshots, bugle call and bird chirps, and gibberish Animalese voices for the cast, all synthesized in code (engine chip synth); no audio files\",\n \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode: reticles sent between up to four copies; progress and a single result reported to the hub\",\n \"testing\": \"Node tests (node tests/run.mjs) drive the game with game.advance and game.debug, including a scripted whole-campaign playthrough; a Chromium pass over every screen (tests/browser.py); the AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players with latency, jitter and loss\",\n \"research\": \"Read the Big Buck Hunter and Big Buck Hunter Pro pages during planning (PLAN.md section 1.1); nothing new searched while building\",\n \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium for the browser checks; browser for the player unknown\",\n \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n \"usage\": \"unknown\",\n})\nf['testingFeedback'] = [\n \"About 9 game issues: 1 critical (the results screen threw after the last segment, so a finished Hunt-Off showed the engine's error panel and could not be saved); 8 smaller (prompt glyphs showing as '?', a caption over the rifle panel, Dev mode rows running into the hint line, antlers above the Shot Chart frame, an empty bar on the doe-rule choice, a shot-into-a-doe bug that benched the attract bot's gun, a crash when firing outside a site, and menu idle not starting attract). Most were found in the browser pass and screenshots.\",\n \"Critical: the results-screen crash, found by a screenshot after the campaign ended, not by the Node tests, which had passed. Game-breaking for the campaign ending; fixed and covered by the browser pass.\",\n \"Most helpful: the browser pass that opens every screen and takes screenshots. It caught the crash and the visual faults the Node checks could not see.\",\n \"Least helpful: the same-seed determinism check. It only confirms the seeded streams repeat, and passed on the first run. The AI Hub harness was more useful: it checked the real protocol with a real client.\",\n]\nf['engineFeedback'] = [\n \"Liked most: the overlay and pixel primitives (r.overlay with px.rect, poly, ell and font.text) made a custom pseudo-3D scene easy; and the standard pause, settings, controls and full screen menus came free.\",\n \"Stuck or guessed wrong: scene changes fade, so a key sent right after one lands on the old scene (tests need about 0.6 s of settling); a scripted tap sets the last device to touch, so input.label() shows action names; the font has no middle dot or en dash, so they print as '?'. I guessed E.mix and E.font.wrap from the index and confirmed both by running them.\",\n \"Most important thing built myself: the hunt itself. The landscape painter, the animal rigs, the hit zones and shot resolution, the pump and chamber model, the bot, the x-ray Shot Chart and the bonus games. The engine's depth, lighting and camera were bypassed for an overlay-drawn scene.\",\n \"Hardest part: fitting an on-rails, screen-space shooter into an engine built around its camera views and lit scenes; the overlay gets no depth sort, lighting or shadows for free.\",\n \"Changes to the engine: none. The engine file is the handoff copy, unmodified.\",\n \"One change I'd make: label() should fall back to the keyboard's names when the last device is a scripted tap, and the font should cover the middle dot and en dash.\",\n]\nf['promptFeedback'] = [\n \"Liked most: the explicit core loop, the one-line deliverable names, and the testing rules (game.advance, game.debug, one command that prints only failures). They made the work concrete.\",\n \"Confusing: PLAN.md names a different title and dev folder from TASK.md, and describes about 30 source files and a 17-minute, three-hunt game with a voxel renderer. TASK.md wins on conflicts, but the scale was hard to reconcile with one session, so I built the plan's systems in a smaller form.\",\n \"Hardest: keeping to the plan's scope while finishing a complete, playable slice in one session, and writing the usage and feedback answers accurately without measurements.\",\n \"Change: say up front how much of the plan is required versus illustrative, give a scope budget for one session, and say whether the title should come from the plan or be drawn fresh.\",\n]\nf['aiHub'].update({\n \"series\": \"Big Buck Hunter\",\n \"players\": \"1-4\",\n \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\"],\n \"controls\": \"Aim: mouse or left stick. Shoot: click, Space or R2. Pump: R or Square. Scope: hold Shift or right click. Call: C or Triangle.\"\n})\njson.dump(f, open(p,'w'), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('feedback written')\nEOF\nnode build/build.mjs && timeout 600 node tests/run.mjs | tail -3 && python3 -c \"import json; j=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json')); print(sorted(j.keys())); print(len(j['testingFeedback']), len(j['engineFeedback']), len(j['promptFeedback']))\"","description":"Write final feedback, rebuild, rerun tests, validate interview"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01UpfvzMRf7X14RhsYqxc86U":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-054528__x4cdb93/work/BigBuckHunterHoedown-BigBuckHunterPro-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-054528"}}}
