{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghxPNP8pRhkbW7hNEjVG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The two gaps you flagged are only partly closed, and I'm not claiming the goal is fully met.\n\n**Animation.** The animal motion that changes over time now runs on the engine's tween system. Falls use `outBounce`, the head going down to graze uses `outCubic`, and the bonus snowman's pop uses `outBack`. The hand-stepped versions are gone. What I still draw myself is the gait, the grazing and wing poses, and the critter shapes, from continuous values. The engine's Humanoid and Quadruped rigs are not used. I judged them a poor fit for the animals, but that is a judgment call, and you may not accept it.\n\n**Controller and touch.** The gamepad is tested through the engine's input map. Scripted presses on RT (fire), Square (pump) and the button glyph labels (✕ for PlayStation, A for Xbox) all pass. The touch-only screen is tested only with a stubbed device query. Real gamepad and touch hardware were not available here. So the 10-foot, controller-first UI is not confirmed on a real controller or touch device. That needs a manual check.\n\n**Checks.** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 198 checks. The AI Hub harness passes at 2 players and at 4 players under latency, jitter and loss. The bundle and `exit-interview.json` are in the work root, and the interview parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:45:28\n- **Source:** Big Buck Hunter Pro\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade light-gun hunting shooter with a trophy encounter, bonus games, a practice range, and a hot-seat party mode. First person on rails over a pseudo-3D landscape, with an x-ray Shot Chart and 2D menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (unmodified), AI Hub client lib/hub session.js 1.4.0 (verbatim), vanilla JavaScript, Node 24, Playwright with Chromium\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's retro-modern pixel style, with landscapes, animals and paper targets painted in code\n- **Animation:** Engine tweens for falls, grazing heads and bonus pop-ups. Gait, poses and critter shapes are drawn in my own painters; the engine's rigs were not used.\n- **Audio:** Bluegrass chiptune songs, gunshots, bugle and bird calls, and Animalese voices, all synthesized\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs` (198 checks: a scripted campaign, range, party, labs, tweens, gamepad presses through the input map, and a Chromium pass); the AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players under stress. Physical gamepad and touch hardware not tested.\n- **Research:** Planning-stage reading of the Big Buck Hunter and Big Buck Hunter Pro pages (PLAN.md §1.1)\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); the player's browser and controller unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9 game issues in the first build, plus a few in the new modes. Most were visual faults and one results-screen crash.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** One critical in the first build: the results screen crashed after the last segment. Fixed and covered by the browser pass.\n- **Most helpful test:** The Chromium pass over every screen, which caught the crash and the visual faults.\n- **Least helpful test:** The same-seed determinism check, which only confirms the seeded streams repeat.\n- **Not tested:** Physical gamepads and touch devices. The gamepad path is tested through the engine's input map, and the touch-only screen through a stubbed device query.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The overlay and pixel primitives made a custom scene easy. The tweens made the falls and pops simple to drive.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Scene changes fade, so keys sent right after one hit the old scene. A scripted tap marks the device as \"touch\", which makes `input.label()` show action names. The font lacks the middle dot and en dash.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** The hunt: landscape, animals, hit zones, the pump model, the bot, the Shot Chart, the range, the party mode, and the labs.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting an on-rails, screen-space shooter into an engine built around camera views and lit scenes.\n- **Engine changes:** None. The engine file is the handoff copy, unmodified.\n- **One change I'd make:** Make `label()` fall back to keyboard names after a scripted tap, and cover the middle dot and en dash in the font.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The explicit core loop, the exact deliverable names, and the testing rules.\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md names a different title and dev folder from TASK.md, and describes far more than one session's worth of work. It doesn't say which parts are required, so \"feature-complete\" and \"every feature in the plan\" are hard to tell apart.\n- **Hardest:** Finishing the plan's systems in one session, and answering the usage and feedback questions honestly without measurements.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark which plan features are required and which are optional, and say whether local multiplayer must be simultaneous. Include a way to verify hardware-only requirements, such as a controller, from a headless environment."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1832,"cache_read_input_tokens":390743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1832},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"799c6357-620a-439f-ad68-1731060eb345","uuid":"2e6b258e-be7b-475c-a969-fae1572e1563","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:20:05.624Z","request_id":"req_011CghxPMya8cAuMn9tGwVLJ"}
