{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghxg3NrwGfgdtftuw6fH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The animals now run on a four-legged rig, and I've checked it in the browser. One requirement still can't be met from this machine: the controller-first UI needs a real gamepad and touch device, and I have neither. So I can't honestly report every TASK.md feature as verified.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Animals:** deer, elk, moose, cow, raccoon and skunk share one four-legged rig in `src/12-rig.js`. It takes the engine's convention: `update(dt, state)` poses it from speed, state and the head tween, and `draw` only paints. The old one-off painters are gone.\n- **Engine:** the engine ships only a Humanoid and a Blob, so the rig isn't the engine's own. Falls, grazing heads and the bonus snowman's pop use the engine's tweens.\n- **Checks:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 205 checks, including the browser pass. The AI Hub harness passes at 2 and 4 players under stress. The bundle and `exit-interview.json` are in the work root, and the interview parses.\n\n**Still open**\n- The controller-first UI on real hardware. The gamepad path is tested only through the engine's input map, and the touch-only screen only with a stubbed device query. Someone needs to run a real controller and a touch device before this can be called verified.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:45:28\n- **Source:** Big Buck Hunter Pro\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade light-gun hunting shooter with a trophy encounter, bonus games, a practice range, and a hot-seat party mode. First person on rails over a pseudo-3D landscape, with an x-ray Shot Chart and 2D menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (unmodified), AI Hub client lib/hub session.js 1.4.0 (verbatim), vanilla JavaScript, Node 24, Playwright with Chromium\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's retro-modern pixel style, with landscapes, animals and paper targets painted in code\n- **Animation:** Engine tweens for falls, grazing heads and bonus pop-ups. Animals share a four-legged rig written to the engine's rig convention; the engine ships no quadruped rig, and its Humanoid and Blob were not used for the animals.\n- **Audio:** Bluegrass chiptune songs, gunshots, bugle and bird calls, and Animalese voices, all synthesized\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs` (205 checks: a scripted campaign, the range, party turns, the labs, tweens, gamepad presses through the input map, and a Chromium pass); the AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players under stress. Physical gamepad and touch hardware not tested.\n- **Research:** Planning-stage reading of the Big Buck Hunter and Big Buck Hunter Pro pages (PLAN.md §1.1)\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); the player's browser and controller unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9 game issues in the first build, plus a few in the new modes. Most were visual faults, plus one results-screen crash.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** One critical in the first build: the results screen crashed after the last segment. Fixed and covered by the browser pass.\n- **Most helpful test:** The Chromium pass over every screen, which caught the crash and the visual faults.\n- **Least helpful test:** The same-seed determinism check, which only confirms the seeded streams repeat.\n- **Not tested:** Physical gamepads and touch devices. The gamepad path is tested through the engine's input map, and the touch-only screen through a stubbed device query.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The overlay and pixel primitives made a custom scene easy. The tweens made falls and pop-ups simple to drive.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Scene changes fade, so keys sent right after one hit the old scene. A scripted tap marks the device as \"touch\", which makes `input.label()` show action names. The font lacks the middle dot and en dash. The engine ships no quadruped rig.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** The hunt: landscape, animals, the four-legged rig, hit zones, the pump model, the bot, the Shot Chart, the range, the party mode, and the labs.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting an on-rails, screen-space shooter into an engine built around camera views and lit scenes, with no four-legged rig to start from.\n- **Engine changes:** None. The engine file is the handoff copy, unmodified. The quadruped rig is in the game's source.\n- **One change I'd make:** Ship a quadruped rig. Make `label()` fall back to keyboard names after a scripted tap, and cover the middle dot and en dash in the font.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The explicit core loop, the exact deliverable names, and the testing rules.\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md names a different title and dev folder from TASK.md, and describes far more than one session's worth of work. It doesn't say which parts are required, so \"feature-complete\" and \"every feature in the plan\" are hard to tell apart.\n- **Hardest:** Finishing the plan's systems in one session, and answering the usage and feedback questions honestly without measurements.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark which plan features are required and which are optional. Say whether local multiplayer must be simultaneous. Say how hardware-only requirements, such as a real controller, should be verified when the agent has no hardware."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1661,"cache_read_input_tokens":410540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1661},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"799c6357-620a-439f-ad68-1731060eb345","uuid":"85f2fdba-f63c-42f0-ba0a-eea8b2d3c10e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:23:51.240Z","request_id":"req_011Cghxg341Y7W4b7iYhisq2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not satisfied. The bundle and exit-interview.json exist, the interview parses, and all four report sections are present. But the final message itself says the controller-first UI 'still can't be met from this machine' and 'is not confirmed on a real controller or touch device', so TASK.md's 10-foot controller-first requirement lacks evidence, and the 'every feature in TASK.md is implemented' clause is not established. The animals now use a custom four-legged rig, which is a judgement call on the 'engine's native animation system as the base' requirement rather than a clear failure, but the unverified hardware UI alone blocks the condition."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"799c6357-620a-439f-ad68-1731060eb345","uuid":"d78df660-239a-4339-abfe-3f04f049ad1b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:23:52.932Z","isSynthetic":true}
