{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghxvZP38dhHZK85hkpkb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've reached the limit of what I can verify, so I'm stopping without further changes. The stop condition requires two things I can't produce from this machine:\n\n1. **Controller-first UI on real hardware.** Confirming it needs a physical gamepad and a touch device. The simulated checks I ran cover the browser path, not the hardware.\n2. **Engine's native animation system for the animals.** The engine ships only a Humanoid and a Blob. The animals use a four-legged rig I wrote in the game's source, following the engine's convention. That is a judgement call against the TASK.md wording, not a verified match to it.\n\nEverything else in TASK.md is built and tested: `node tests/run.mjs` passes 206 checks, and the AI Hub harness passes at 2 and 4 players.\n\n**To close this out, you choose one:**\n- Run the controller and touch pass yourself and send me what breaks. I'll fix it.\n- Accept the build with the controller UI and the animal rig marked unverified or non-native.\n- Give me a different animation approach for the animals, such as using the engine's Humanoid for the cast only and keeping the animals hand-drawn.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:45:28\n- **Source:** Big Buck Hunter Pro\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade light-gun hunting shooter with a trophy encounter, bonus games, a practice range, and a hot-seat party mode. First person on rails over a pseudo-3D landscape, with an x-ray Shot Chart and 2D menus.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (unmodified), AI Hub client lib/hub session.js 1.4.0 (verbatim), vanilla JavaScript, Node 24, Playwright with Chromium\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's retro-modern pixel style, with landscapes, animals and paper targets painted in code\n- **Animation:** Engine tweens for falls, grazing heads and bonus pop-ups. Animals share a four-legged rig written to the engine's rig convention, since the engine ships only a Humanoid and a Blob.\n- **Audio:** Bluegrass chiptune songs, gunshots, bugle and bird calls, and Animalese voices, all synthesized\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs` (206 checks), including a simulated gamepad and touch-only device in Chromium and the AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players. No physical controller or touch device.\n- **Research:** Planning-stage reading of the Big Buck Hunter and Big Buck Hunter Pro pages (PLAN.md §1.1)\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); the player's browser and controller unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 9 game issues in the first build, plus a few in the new modes. Most were visual faults, plus one results-screen crash.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** One in the first build: the results screen crashed after the last segment. Fixed and covered by the browser pass.\n- **Most helpful test:** The Chromium pass over every screen, which caught the crash and the visual faults.\n- **Least helpful test:** The same-seed determinism check, which only confirms the seeded streams repeat.\n- **Not tested:** Physical gamepads and touch devices. The simulated pass checks the browser path, not the hardware.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The overlay and pixel primitives made a custom scene easy. The tweens made falls and pop-ups simple to drive.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Scene changes fade, so keys sent right after one hit the old scene. A scripted tap marks the device as \"touch\", which makes `input.label()` show action names. The font lacks the middle dot and en dash. The engine ships no quadruped rig.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** The hunt: landscape, animals, the four-legged rig, hit zones, the pump model, the bot, the Shot Chart, the range, the party mode, and the labs.\n- **Hardest part:** Fitting an on-rails, screen-space shooter into an engine built around camera views and lit scenes, with no four-legged rig to start from.\n- **Engine changes:** None. The engine file is the handoff copy, unmodified. The quadruped rig is in the game's source.\n- **One change I'd make:** Ship a quadruped rig. Make `label()` fall back to keyboard names after a scripted tap, and cover the middle dot and en dash in the font.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The explicit core loop, the exact deliverable names, and the testing rules.\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md names a different title and dev folder from TASK.md, and describes far more than one session's worth of work. It doesn't say which parts are required, so \"feature-complete\" and \"every feature in the plan\" are hard to tell apart.\n- **Hardest:** Finishing the plan's systems in one session, and answering the usage and feedback questions honestly without measurements.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark which plan features are required and which are optional. Say whether local multiplayer must be simultaneous. Say how hardware-only requirements should be verified when the agent has no hardware."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2518,"cache_read_input_tokens":421449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2518},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"799c6357-620a-439f-ad68-1731060eb345","uuid":"8aa66067-26b1-492c-99b7-079db0b18ba8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:27:07.917Z","request_id":"req_011CghxvYv1kVEkGaQbuU6c7"}
